t the macbook pros will  have a notch and he was right as for the  keyboard i expect it to also feature  white keys and before you say it's going  to be really dirty don't forget that the  magic keyboard on the imac comes with  white keys and i also think that the  keyboard will be off-white so it matches  the new macbook pro design as you can  see this one comes in a beautiful light  blue finish straight from the stand of  the blue 24 inch imac which will be very  consumer friendly and as for the ports i  expected to get the max a3 connector on  the left side a thunderbolt 4 port on  each side and a headphone jack on the  right and on the bottom you could see a  clean macbook air engraving and four  feet just like the pro models and if  you're interested in the simple and  clean blue macbook wallpaper i'll leave  a link to it in the video description  down below and while you're there go  ahead hit that subscribe button to help  us reach our goal of 1 million  subscribers we would greatly appreciate  it now in terms of the release date i  think that mark's recent leak has  finally put the spring event release  rumor to rest he said that at least four  new macs powered by m2 chips are  launching later this year after apple  finishes releasing its final max with  the m1 pro and m1 max chips yep that is  right no m2 chip reveal until the last  of the m1 powered macs are released and  if you didn't know this already apple is  still selling both the intel based  high-end mac mini and the 27-inch imac  and both of those need to be switched  over to apple silicon before the m2  chips can be released so before i get  into when we can expect the m2 max to be  revealed we've got to cover those high  end m1 bass max first when we first saw  the leaked design of the m1 mac mini  from jon proster last year he said that  it could be coming as soon as the end of  2021  and even dylan dkt was confident that  the mac mini would launch alongside the  new 14 and 16 inch macbook pros but  unfortunately that didn't happen and his  reasoning for it was that apple wanted  the macbook pros to get all of the  attention to boost sales even though the  mac mini was likely ready at the time  and in mark german's report over the  weekend he confirmed that at least one  new mac will be revealed at the event  next month so with all of that said i  can almost 100 guarantee that it's gonna  be a mac mini for sure because the imac  side of things isn't looking too certain  ross young recently came out and said  that apple is unfortunately delaying the  release of their imac pro potentially as  late as august or september and this  actually came after a controversial  tweet from dylan dkt where he said that  there have been some concerns about the  shipping date of the imac pro and also  said that a september launch was the  worst case scenario so i think that it  totally makes sense for apple to reveal  the imac pro alongside the apple silicon  mac pro at their wwdc event in june and  this makes sense because both machines  are expected to come with the new  powerful m1 based chip either the 12  core chip that dylan leaked or the 20  core m1 max duo which literally means  two m1 max dies combined into one using  the high bandwidth fabric however we  asked ross young if there is a  possibility the apple could still  release a regular 27 inch imac in the  spring with just the same options of the  m1 pro and m1 max chips like we have in  the current macbook pros and he said he  wasn't sure about this because he was  only tracking imac pro models so with  that said we could still see a 2 000 27  inch mac model at the spring event  alongside the mac mini but it is not for  certain just yet now on top of all of  that mark also said something quite  controversial in his weekend report he  says that the technology to embed face  id into macbook displays doesn't exist  so if face id comes to the mac he thinks  that it will come on an imac or an  external monitor first and apple has  definitely been working on this but time  will tell if they launch it now if you  already didn't know 95 mac found code in  a mac os beta way back in 2020 showing  that they are working on it so in my  opinion i think it makes total sense for  this feature to be launched with the new  imac pro this year especially since we  just saw some new apple patents filed  concerning face id coming to the imac  but as far as the macbook side of things  even though we have that notch i don't  think we will see it until 2023 when  apple launches the m2 pro macbook pros  with a thinner face id module now the  last thing that i want to mention from  mark's weekend report is that the new  entry level m2 macbook pro will not be  getting a pro motion display which isn't  what we were expecting so what this  could mean is that it only comes with a  regular lcd display  but no i do not think that makes sense  because all of the leaks within the last  year pointed to the new redesigned  macbook air getting a mini led display  just like the current pro models that  are much more expensive so this means  that the new m2 entry-level macbook pro  that a lot of people have been waiting  for with the lower budget also needs  mini led so simply likely that the new  pro will have mini led but will lack pro  motion so if you want that sweet 120  hertz you will have to go for at least a  2 000 macbook pro which is a pretty  smart roof move from apple standpoint to  differentiate it and get people to spend  more money and now let's finish off with  when we will be getting the new m2 max  now i fully believe that they absolutely  must be revealed at an apple event after  all of the m1 base max are revealed  which i don't think will happen until  wwdc when apple reveals either the new  imac pro or the new mac pro or both so  with that said the only remaining option  would be the october event which is when  apple usually shows off their new mac  products and in my opinion there is a  chance that they could release all four  of them at once or at least within a  couple months of each other which sounds  a bit odd but i expect most of them to  be the simple chip spec updates like the  m2 mac mini and the 24 inch m2 imac the  entry level macbook pro will literally  just be a cheaper version of the current  m1 pro 14-ish macbook pro packed with an  m2 chip but lacking pro motion and  coming with less storage and ram at that  base price and remember the m2 chip will  be weaker than an m1 pro the redesigned  macbook air will be the only one that  will come with totally new features and  design changes like in these recent  renders with the white bezels and new  colors and all so with all that said let  me quickly run through the expected mac  lineup one more time we have the m1 pro  and max mac mini at the event next month  potentially alongside a matching new 27  imac then we have both the imac pro and  the mac pro at wwdc in june just to  finish out the two-year apple silicon  transition then we've got all of the m2  max at apple's october event with apple  potentially delaying one or two of them  by a month or two if they don't want to  release all four at once and there you  have it that is apple's updated 2022 mac  lineup which we can expect based on mark  german's recent bombshell report so  hopefully you enjoyed this video and if  you totally disagree with any of this  comment your thoughts down below we want  to hear your guys opinion if you enjoyed  it click that circle above to subscribe  to see more videos like this one and  help us reach our goal of 1 million  subscribers check out one of those great  videos right over there that's been max  and i'll see you in the next video  [Music]  you

